en more great news  according to the apple analyst ming chi  quo the iphone 14 will be upgraded from  a six element lens to a staggering seven  element lens in its telephoto camera  moreover the new camera will have 8k  video recording capabilities it's crow's  sincere belief that this 8k video  recording feature will give a great user  experience as the iphone recorded videos  can be displayed on the tv now with this  marvelous resolution we can expect to  create pictures and videos better suited  to apple's new augmented and mixed  reality devices 2. the design change  according to renders and some cad files  recently leaked by reporters it is now  almost certain that apple will get rid  of the notch the new design that will  replace the notch will be a hole punch  and pill-shaped cutout this cutout will  bring back much of the area that the  notch took up and who knows we might  even see a battery percentage indicator  a few updates down the line now the  notch has been continuously getting  upgrades since the iphone x but the fact  of the matter is that in terms of screen  to body ratio the notch just could not  compete with what the androids were  offering phones with in-display  fingerprint scanners and motorized  camera units were offering way higher  screen to body ratios and it seems like  apple has finally decided to up its game  too the new phone is going to have a  thicker chassis now what does that mean  for the latest elegant design apparently  the lenses led flash and lidar scanner  will be lying flush with the rear glass  and let me tell you this sort of  non-protruding camera design hasn't been  seen since the very initial days of the  iphone on top of this the flush camera  might even feature round volume buttons  that are a great throwback to the  buttons from previous iphone 4 and  iphone 5 models now in case you're  wondering no the lack of a notch does  not mean that apple will be getting rid  of face id the pill-shaped cutout is for  the ir sc